cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the archived version and acknowledge the underlying CR2MET data product."
title: "Hybrid Hidden Markov–Copula Precipitation Framework"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Herrera-Marín"
    given-names: "Mauricio"
    affiliation: "Universidad del Desarrollo"
abstract: >-
  Research code and a compressed derived precipitation dataset supporting
  evaluation of a hybrid non-homogeneous Hidden Markov Model (nHMM),
  Dynamic Time Warping (DTW) zones, state-conditional regular vine copulas,
  and Generalized Pareto (GPD) tails for Chilean rainfall regimes.
  Includes an R simulation and validation script for May–August 2022
  based on processed historical inputs.
keywords:
  - precipitation
  - Chile
  - non-homogeneous Hidden Markov models
  - vine copulas
  - extreme precipitation
  - stochastic weather simulation
  - hydroclimate
repository-code: "https://github.com/mauricio-herrera/hybrid-nhmm-copula-precipitation-framework"
url: "https://github.com/mauricio-herrera/hybrid-nhmm-copula-precipitation-framework"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-10-12"
